## About the UN

The United Nations is an intergovernmental organisation founded in 1945. Through its organs and specialised agencies, the UN adopts conventions, recommendations and technical regulations that member states transpose nationally.

## Role in the regulatory landscape

UN conventions and model regulations underpin international and national regulatory frameworks, including the transport of dangerous goods, human rights and the Globally Harmonized System for chemicals (GHS).
